# EVERY LAYER WHOSE HOLDER SHARES ARE ALL STATED, BESIDE THE MAGNITUDE THEY MUST ADD UP TO.
# One row per examined layer, `violates` where the sum misses.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE RULE: the stated shares sum to the magnitude of the remainder. H is a DISTRIBUTION,
#    so its row must account for the whole of what there was to bear -- no more, no less.
#
# ⛔⛔ ONE UNSTATED SHARE SUSPENDS THE CHECK RATHER THAN BREAKING IT, and the difference is
#    the whole discipline. If a filer says one party's share is `unmeasured`, the sum is
#    UNKNOWN -- not wrong. Treating the absence as a zero would manufacture a shortfall and
#    report the document for a defect the checker introduced.
# ⛔⛔⛔ THE UNIT GUARD IS THE HALF THIS RULE USED TO BE MISSING, AND ITS OWN SITE HAD IT.
#    arithmetic/shares_sum.sqlc reports `not comparable` where a holder's share is quoted in a
#    unit other than its layer's; this rule had no such branch and would have summed across
#    units and compared the total to |r|. H is a distribution over the magnitude of `r`, so a
#    share in a foreign unit is not a smaller share, it is not a share of this at all.
#    arithmetic/roster.sqlc records `guarded_by = NULL` for that site: no unit rule stands there,
#    which left this check as the only thing between it and a wrong number. It agreed with the
#    site on today's corpus only because no such document exists yet.
# ⭐⭐⭐ AND IT READS THE WHOLE INTERVAL, NOT THE MIDDLE NUMBER. This compared `abs(r_mode)`
#    against `shares_mode` and nothing else, in a model whose entire thesis is that a quantity
#    is a RANGE. Demonstrated 2026-09-06: widening `enterprise-contract/support-cover`'s only
#    share from [21, 50, 76] to [21, 50, 300] -- on a layer whose whole nameplate is 168 -- was
#    accepted by all 24 rules, because the mode did not move. Three other rules still do
#    arithmetic on the mode alone.
#
# ⛔⛔ CONTAINMENT AT THE ENDS AND EQUALITY AT THE MODE, AND THE ASYMMETRY IS NOT A COMPROMISE.
#    Requiring equality at the ends would accuse a MORE careful filing. Checked over every
#    layer this rule examines: 21 of 22 have shares equal to the magnitude at all three points,
#    and one does not -- `merge-holding-composition/compute`, whose shares [1414, 4085.6] sit
#    INSIDE a magnitude of [1092, 4198.8]. That is the cross-unit fusion, and a narrower
#    interval is what composing per-part and converting gives you: `(Σn) − (Σd)` treats the two
#    sums as independent, and `Σ(nᵢ − dᵢ)` does not. The naive bound is the loose one, so a
#    rule demanding equality with it would report the accurate document.
#
# ⭐ |r| OVER AN INTERVAL NEEDS THE STRADDLE CASE. Where `r` crosses zero the magnitude reaches
#   0, which is the transition fit stated as arithmetic: short at the top of the demand range
#   and spare at the bottom, both at once. Taking `least(|r_low|, |r_high|)` there would invent
#   a floor the layer does not have.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:holder summed against |r| at the mode, via entries/holder_totals.sqlc.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT x.filing, x.layer,
           abs(x.shares - x.magnitude) > 1e-9
           OR x.shares_low  < x.mag_low  - 1e-9
           OR x.shares_high > x.mag_high + 1e-9                       AS violates,
           format('shares [%s, %s, %s] against a magnitude of [%s, %s, %s]',
                  x.shares_low, x.shares, x.shares_high,
                  x.mag_low, x.magnitude, x.mag_high)                 AS detail
    FROM (
        SELECT r.filing, r.layer,
               abs(r.r_mode)  AS magnitude,
               h.shares_mode  AS shares,
               h.shares_low, h.shares_high,
               -- ⭐ |r| OVER AN INTERVAL, AND THE STRADDLE IS THE CASE THAT NEEDS SAYING. A
               --   remainder whose range crosses zero has a magnitude that reaches 0, which is
               --   the transition fit: short at the top of the demand range and spare at the
               --   bottom, both at once.
               CASE WHEN r.r_low <= 0 AND r.r_high >= 0 THEN 0
                    ELSE least(abs(r.r_low), abs(r.r_high)) END       AS mag_low,
               greatest(abs(r.r_low), abs(r.r_high))                  AS mag_high
        FROM      (
            :compose(layers/remainder.sqlc)
        ) r
        JOIN      (
            :compose(entries/holder_totals.sqlc)
        ) h USING (filing, layer)
        WHERE h.unstated = 0
          AND h.share_units = ARRAY[r.unit]
    ) x
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'shares_do_not_sum'
